# Product brief guide

## Core fields

1. Brand + product name
2. Product details / USP
3. Target audience
4. Narration: yes/no
5. Wardrobe
6. Location
7. Requested language / dialect
8. Product or content link
9. Mode: Normal / Deep Research
10. Character and product reference images

## Product facts to clarify when relevant

Features, materials, dimensions, ingredients, texture, function, usage, packaging, variants, price, shipping, limitations, safety information, and differentiators.

## Emotional detail prompts

Ask about relatable use situations, friction, concerns, desired feelings, and what a satisfying experience would look like. Keep emotional framing grounded and non-manipulative.

## Evidence discipline

Label information as user-provided, externally verified, or creative direction. Do not infer exact product specifications from a category name or an unclear photo.
